{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>All the firstborn males that are born of your herd and of your flock you shall sanctify to HaShem your Elohim.</b> Even though the firstborn is holy of itself, for the Holy One, blessed be He, made sanctity depend on the opening of the womb, He nonetheless said 'you shall sanctify' by mouth, and it is a commandment to sanctify it by calling a name over it. And the verse that says (Leviticus 27:26) ״אך בכור אשר יבכר לה' וגו' לא יקדיש איש אותו״ — 'Only the firstborn that is firstborn to HaShem… no man shall sanctify it' — its reason is that one should not sanctify it for another offering."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:32.229974293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}